  "_note": [
    "MEASURED LIVE, and the dirty state is reached by actually editing a token:",
    "Brand -> Tokens -> color -> `color-action` -> put a different hex in the Light",
    "value field. The panel is dirty because a token really changed, not because a",
    "fixture said so, and the root then shows what 154:78 draws \u2014 the amber dot on",
    "the Tokens row and the Save bar at the foot.",
    "",
    "NOT reached by applying a starter, and that is a FINDING, not a preference.",
    "152:137's own prototype hotspot (1670:7235) says a starter click lands here,",
    "and it does raise the dirty flag \u2014 but in Beginner mode, which is the panel's",
    "default, it also EMPTIES the screen this board draws. `stageTokens` REPLACES",
    "the colour registry with the starter's nine tokens, not one of which carries",
    "`semanticKind` (grep the six files under design-system/starters \u2014 zero hits),",
    "and `filterTokensByMode(..., \"beginner\")` keeps only tokens that do. So after",
    "applying Stripe Blue the Brand preview renders no swatches at all and the",
    "Tokens row loses its count, against a board that draws four swatches and",
    "`Tokens 4`. Measured: both `brand-preview-swatches` and",
    "`brand-row-count-tokens` resolved to 0 elements on that path.",
    "Not fixed here: the repair is metadata on 54 starter tokens across six files,",
    "and adding `semanticKind` also feeds the linter's `semantic-needs-alias` rule",
    "(those tokens carry no `aliasOf`), so it is a product change with a lint",
    "consequence rather than a conformance edit. Reported for the founder.",
    "",
    "WHAT THE BOARD WON:",
    "  save bar type    154:128 sets 12/18 for the whole bar; the status line and",
    "                   both actions shipped at 11 with the line inherited, a size",
    "                   below every other label in the panel.",
    "  Save weight      `font-medium` -> `font-normal`. 154:131 is Inter Regular",
    "                   like its two neighbours; the medium weight made `Save` the",
    "                   only bold word on a bar the board draws in one voice.",
    "  Plus the whole root chassis \u2014 see surfaces/brand-lint-warnings.json.",
    "",
    "FIXED ALONG THE WAY, found by the contrast sweep rather than by eye: hovering",
    "the SELECTED segment of the Beginner/Pro toggle repainted it `gray-100` under",
    "`text-white` \u2014 flowbite's `color=\"light\"` theme carries `hover:bg-gray-100`,",
    "and a hover variant beats a plain `bg-*` utility. The label measured 1.1:1 and",
    "vanished. This recipe's click path happens to park the pointer there, which is",
    "the only reason anything ever looked.",
    "",
    "NOT JOINED: 154:78 itself (the drawer's edge) and 1691:7280 (the preview",
    "band's 82px Figma text-metric height) \u2014 see brand-lint-warnings.json.",
    "",
    "The last step re-waits for `brand-save-bar-save` after the walk back. One run in four reached the root CLEAN, and the cause is worth writing down: `Composer.markDirty()` emits `project:changed` on every logical project modification, and `TokensSection`'s handler for it calls `resetAll(...)` -> `resetFromSaved`, which moves savedTokens too and therefore DISCARDS staged brand edits. DesignSystemTab's own handlers for the neighbouring events (`settings:change`, `history:undo/redo`) guard on `isDirtyRef` and warn instead, for exactly this reason; TokensSection's does not. Without this step the flake reads as a MISSING target instead of a failed step.",
    "",
    "CHECK-BOARD-COPY: the same four leads as brand-lint-warnings.json, triaged",
    "there \u2014 `components` (two boards disagree), `beginner`/`pro` (the documented",
    "toggle), and 154:132's Beginner footnote."
  ]
}